    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Stigma is the second studio album by EMF, released in 1992 on Parlophone. Coming after the huge success of Schubert Dip, it keeps the band’s blend of electronic textures, rock guitar work, and pop instinct, but shifts into a darker, more mysterious mood than its predecessor.\n\nThe album showed EMF moving away from the immediate party-anthem feel of “Unbelievable” toward heavier, more introspective material, with a stronger rock edge and less obvious pop sheen. Across its running time, Stigma reflects the early-1990s alternative dance scene while also pushing the band into tougher, moodier territory, making it an important statement of growth rather than a repeat of their debut’s formula.",
